  "body": "Part of #866.\n\n**What the reporter saw:** on Setup2's page,\n- the radio \"Active setup - new operations and furniture join it\" - \"furniture\" is our in-code word for a setup's stock, WCS and fixtures, and read like an AI hallucination;\n- the refusal \"the program sim carries the machined body only through flips over X or Y and quarter turns about Z ...; this turn would re-sample the body at the grid pitch\", which names neither the turn nor a way out in user words.\n\n**Fix:**\n- The radio reads \"Active setup - new operations go into it, and the Stock and Work offset pages edit it\"; the Setups page footer drops \"furniture\" too.\n- `CARRY_TURN_REFUSAL` (kept, by name) now reads \"the stock simulation can carry machined stock only through a flip over X or Y or a quarter turn about Z (turns that keep the tool axis vertical) - any other turn would have to re-sample the stock and lose its detail\".\n- The carry refusal names the turn between the two setups: \"'Setup2' holds the part turned X -90°, Y 0°, Z 0° from how 'Setup1' holds it\".\n- The page says what to do: choose \"Its own stock\" for this setup, or hold the part the way Setup1 does (a flip over X or Y or a turn about Z also works).\n\n**Done means:** no \"furniture\" on the setup Settings page; the refusal names the turn and the way out, and still contains `CARRY_TURN_REFUSAL`. Pinned by `setup_stock_tests::the_settings_page_has_no_in_code_jargon`, `setup_stock_tests::a_refused_carry_disables_the_option_with_its_reason` and `setup_stock_source::a_side_on_turn_between_setups_is_refused_naming_the_turn`.\n",
